# Files that can change what the automation is allowed to do. A pull request
# touching any of these needs the code owner's approval before it merges, even
# when every check is green. See AGENTS.md.
#
# Everything not listed here is deliberately unowned, so ordinary content and
# code pull requests still auto-merge on green without waiting on a human.
#
# Directory rules are written twice, as `dir/` and `dir/**`. GitHub documents
# the trailing-slash form as owning the directory and its subdirectories; the
# `**` form is belt and braces. Last matching rule wins, and both name the same
# owner, so the duplication is harmless.

/.github/settings.yml      @mchelen
/.github/CODEOWNERS        @mchelen
/.github/workflows/        @mchelen
/.github/workflows/**      @mchelen
/CHARTER.md                @mchelen
